    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="af104445-17be-53db-b6c7-a4f1fe815b7c" activityNameId="e9da8b8d-956d-52ad-b7c8-26afe13eaf9f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Transport, high speed train, Fahrzeug</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Transport, high speed train, Fahrzeug
For rail infrastructure, expenditures and environmental interventions due to construction, renewal and disposal of railway tracks have been allocated based on the train kilometric performance of an average German ICE train 417182 vkm and a life time of  40 years .  For the determination of the train demand the yearly transport performance of ICE trains in Germany was used 97837945 pkm.;
UUID: 28a6ab20-4115-309d-ab4e-858302960c20
Included is the  production, maintenance and disposal of high speed train as well as the construction, maintenance and disposal of the railway tracks. The energy consumption (including 5.033% losses and emission of the train operation are accounted for.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: For vehicle operation all technologies  are included in the average data. Rail construction addresses conventional and modern ballastless beddings.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: 97837945 pkm
Sampling: Statistics 
Extrapolations: Emission, extrapolated from long distance train transport in CH
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_28a6ab20-4115-309d-ab4e-858302960c20.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
